mac/install-mac.sh has no failure ledger, so it always exits 0

The audit gave the Linux installers a failure ledger: safe_exec / record_failure /
record_unsupported feed a tally that install_summary turns into an exit code, so
`make install` can no longer report success with ten broken steps. mac/install-mac.sh
never got that pass.

Current state, measured:

    installer                 safe_exec  record_failure  install_summary
    install-ubuntu.sh                59               5  yes
    install-archlinux.sh            142               2  yes
    install-amazon-linux.sh          36              11  yes
    mac/install-mac.sh                1               0  NO

The single safe_exec is at mac/install-mac.sh:149 (rbenv). Everything else - Homebrew
bootstrap, both brew bundle runs, all eleven sourced common/ modules, the cleanup -
runs bare. The script ends with a log_success and some next-step echoes, so it exits 0
regardless of what failed.

Also worth checking during the same pass: :69-79 only log_warn if Brewfile.arm or
Brewfile.x86 is missing, then carry on having installed none of that package set. That
should be a record_failure.

The work is mechanical and mirrors what was already done three times. It is untouched
only because it cannot be verified from here: macOS cannot be containerized, so
make/test/ covers Ubuntu, Arch, Amazon Linux and Termux and leaves this file to static
review. Whoever has a Mac should do the wrapping and then actually run it once.

make/mac/README.md documents the gap.
